here are some simple grammar notes to  help you  through this lesson uh let's first of  all look at verbs  and there are uh verbs are action words  so when we see the expression command  allevo which means how are you  in fact the franchise the french say how  are you  going so ale is to go  vous vous how you go  and the answer is so this is the same  verb  except here it's you and here it's  i so we notice that the verbs change  depending on the  person whether it is  now how can you remember how the verb  changes  the verb allay to go in the present  tense  that's an awful lot to remember you'll  only gradually get used to it  and start remembering it but remember  you can always  google any verb you can google  present tense valet you can google  french verbs you can google  verb alley and you will find all of the  tenses  and all of the forms of the verbs get  used to using  google so when we see the next question  what is your name we have the verb there  it's  a which is a form of the verb etre which  of course you need to find out  but you can google it you can google the  verb et you can probably google  the verb verb est  now let's move a bit on to nouns you'll  see that we say bonjour  and that's an immediate clue that jewel  is masculine because in french they have  gender masculine and feminine on the  other hand  when we see bun nui that tells us that  me night is feminine  the same here with no no  and that tells us it's a masculine noun  the same is  what is your name because if it's  feminine  it would be ma and the kel  would have e-l-l-e there so that's  something to look forward to but this is  just  a brief start to some aspects of verbs  and nouns  in french
 

